={{ {
  model: 'llama3.1:8b-instruct-q4_K_M',
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'system',
      content: 'You are a classifier for an Architecture pipeline. Analyze the user input and determine the mode, intent, and extract project information.\n\nMODE RULES:\n- mode=chat: For queries, help requests, status checks. Keywords: help, status, list, artifacts, jobs, what, how, show, get, query, ?\n- mode=execute: For creating/building/generating architecture. Keywords: build, create, generate, make, develop, design a, implement\n\nIf input is a single word like "help", "list", "jobs", "status" - it is ALWAYS mode=chat.\nIf input asks a question or requests information - it is mode=chat.\nOnly use mode=execute when user explicitly wants to CREATE or BUILD something new.\n\nPROJECT EXTRACTION (CRITICAL):\n- ALWAYS extract the projectSlug from the input text\n- Look for patterns like "project X", "for X", "X project", or project names in the text\n- The projectSlug should be a lowercase-hyphenated string (e.g., "healthcare-appointment-scheduler")\n- If no project name is found, set projectSlug to null\n\nChat intents: help, status, artifacts, jobs, list\nExecute intents: create, build, generate\n\nOutput JSON only.'    },
    { role: 'user', content: $json.rawInput || $json.requirements }
  ],
  stream: false,
  format: {
    type: 'object',
    required: ['mode', 'intent', 'projectSlug'],
    properties: {
      mode: { type: 'string', enum: ['chat', 'execute'] },
      intent: { type: 'string' },
      projectSlug: { type: 'string', description: 'The project name/slug extracted from the input text, lowercase with hyphens' },
      requirements: { type: 'string' }
    }
  },
  options: { temperature: 0.1 }
} }}

